reducer (feature key `'<%= propertyName %>'`), selectors, effects and `<%= className %>StateModule`.

## Use it in an app

The app must register the root store and effects **once**, then import the feature module:

```ts
import { EffectsModule } from '@ngrx/effects';
import { StoreModule } from '@ngrx/store';
import { <%= className %>StateModule } from '<%= importPath %>';

@NgModule({
  imports: [StoreModule.forRoot({}), EffectsModule.forRoot([]), <%= className %>StateModule],
})
export class AppModule {}
```

```ts
constructor(private readonly store: Store) {}

readonly items$ = this.store.select(select<%= className %>Items);

ngOnInit(): void {
  this.store.dispatch(<%= className %>Actions.load());
}
```

`<%= className %>Effects.load$` returns an empty list as a placeholder — call your API there.

Built as a buildable lib (`nx build <%= projectName %>`).
